<title>UK: Hays wins logistics contract from BP.</title>
<headline>Hays wins logistics contract from BP.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British business services company Hays Plc said on Wednesday it had won a five year logistics contract from British Petroleum Co Plc worth up to 100 million stg.</p>
<p>It said it would supply the logistics expertise for a supply chain for the oil giant, which is reorganising the way it supplies up to 1,000 of its shops across the UK.</p>
<p>Hays said that under the new arrangements, some new 500 new jobs would be created and the new supply chain was expected to produce benefits to BP of some 15 million stg a year.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
